    "body": "In an older version of the canvas spec, the 2D context was unnecessarily spec'ed as being double buffered.  There was a notion of a 'scratch bitmap', which was the back buffer, and 'output bitmap' was the front buffer. Some time ago, I refactored this part of the spec to remove the unecessary double buffering buffering.  I thought of using a single bitmap slot, owned by the canvas, but I was concerned that it would make the spec heavier because it would have to formulated in a way that simultaneously works with OffscreenCanvas and HTMLCanvasElement.\r\n\r\nA possible solution would be to put  the 'context' and 'bitmap' slots into a common base interface (e.g. RenderingContextHost) that is inherrited by both OffscreenCanvas and HTMLCanvasElement.  Then the 2D context prose could refer to the bitmap as the \"context's host's bitmap\".  This way we have a single bitmap slot to rule them all (no shared references).  Anyways, I could not convince myself that this approach made the spec any simpler, and I did not have any better ideas.\r\n\r\nAnother thing to think about is that PaintRenderingContext2D also has dependencies on many of the sub-interfaces of CanvasRenderingContext2D, which we need to be mindful of not breaking when we refactor this part of the spec.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
