    "body": "That is a really good idea IMHO. \r\nWe also need a boolean member to specify whether the bitmap has an alpha channel.\r\n\r\nA current source of incompatibility is that the spec does not define whether bitmaps that do have alpha channels should store color components in alpha pre-multiplied form.  I think this was deliberately left unspecified because different graphics libraries have different limitations.  In some implementations, bitmaps may have a 'premul' bit. I am uncertain whether this should permeate into the spec.  What is clear is that the data in ImageData objects is not premul, but for canvas bitmaps all bets are off.\r\n\r\nThinking ahead: Eventually, this definition of bitmaps will be a good place to put bit-depth and color-space members.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
